Z||000009||maryjane||08-25-2001||07:02 PM||||Galen, hope this is what you want. No idea about gear ratios.<BR>84SE 2.5 auto 150000 miles(eng rebuilt 2mos ago) Tranny stock-never been touched except for fluid/filter chng<BR>2000rpm @55mph<BR>2850rpm @70mph (too much traffic & 60 mph speed limit, couldn't stay at 70 long enough to watch it for long) Pretty good headwind, but level pavement. 95*F,35% hum, 220lb driver, 1/2 donut, haynes manual with 2 missing pages,stock tires & rims, little or no lunar gravitational pull, about a dozen bugs in a/c condensor. Good enough?<BR>Anybody else?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><BR>Don||||reg||1
Z||000010||Galen||08-25-2001||07:25 PM||||okie now this just sucks..<P>someone tell me why my car runs 4k at 70? sticks around 3100 at 55?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/sig.gif">  Ray -    <A HREF="mailto:galen@ezrpg.com">galen@ezrpg.com</A>    - <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>www.FieroLinks.f2s.com</A><BR>AIM: GalenRPG - ICQ: 98668558||||reg||1
Z||000011||maryjane||08-25-2001||07:31 PM||||Tire & rim size maybe. Carrying too many half donuts. Wind beating on pinetree air thingies. Don't know. Never had my eng checked with anything but dashboard tach, it could be wrong, but everyting seems to run allright & we get good mpg.||||reg||1
Z||000012||William Federle||08-25-2001||08:46 PM||||I have a 84 DUKE with a std transmission but from what I've read on the forum, the auto transmissions have a lock up torque convertor - so if your's isn't locking up, your RPM would be higher I'd think. If you can find the solenoid that is activated to lock it up, just unplug it and see if there is any difference. If there isn't then that might be your problem.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Galen||08-25-2001||08:48 PM||||It locks up, sometimes. but it still runs, imo, really high. I did run the tranny almost out of fluid when a line came loose, could this have caused damage that is causing this?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/sig.gif">   Ray -     <A HREF="mailto:galen@ezrpg.com">galen@ezrpg.com</A>     - <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>www.FieroLinks.f2s.com</A> - AIM: GalenRPG - ICQ: 98668558||||reg||1
Z||000014||Songman||08-25-2001||09:55 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Galen:<BR><B>It locks up, sometimes. but it still runs, imo, really high. I did run the tranny almost out of fluid when a line came loose, could this have caused damage that is causing this?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Galen, when I got my T-top the convertor wasn't locking up and it was slipping real bad. I unhooked the lock-up for the drive home from IN. When I got home I was driving it around and the thing finally got to where it wouldn't pull at all! I pulled the dipstick and could smell it before I ever even checked the fluid level. The thing was bone dry! I filled it with fluid and plugged the lock-up back up and haven't had a problem since... when the lock-up was unplugged I ran high rpm's but I don't even think they were as high as you are saying..<P>My 4:10 Indy runs about 4k at 80. Your running way to high if you are 4k at 70. Hate to say it but something is slipping if you ask me...<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||9
Z||000015||Fierowrecker||08-26-2001||11:11 AM||||I pulled the dipstick and could smell it before I ever even checked the fluid level. The thing was bone dry! <P>Ya, sniff the fluid...<BR>If it smells burnt, drain it and replace the filter...<BR>Had to do that twice to my 84...<BR>DO NOT GET IT FLUSHED!!!<BR>My wife had to get her tranny replaced after getting her tranny flushed, trouble is, she had it flushed twice!!!<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000016||goldiron||08-26-2001||11:28 AM||||Just got back from a test run.  Curious as to the answer to your question.  My 87 auto duke runs about 2000 rpm at 50mph and at about 2750 at 70mph.  Car is factory stock everything. Having air on doesn't seem to have much impact.  No idea as to what gear ratio is.||||reg||1
